WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.451
Exercise 6: consumer-driven contracts.

2
00:00:03.501 --> 00:00:08.953
Today, any change to orders_v2 could break you. And the producer cannot see what you use.

3
00:00:09.003 --> 00:00:16.640
Your view needs only five fields of orders_v2. Start from a copy of the producer contract.

4
00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:20.793
This is your contract now. Give it its own ID, the version stays 2.0.0.

5
00:00:20.843 --> 00:00:32.331
Keep only what your view reads: order_id and order_timestamp from orders.

6
00:00:32.381 --> 00:00:38.391
From line_items: order_id, sku, and quantity.

7
00:00:38.441 --> 00:00:44.090
Keep the quantity > 0 check: your data product relies on it.

8
00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:48.489
The result: a small contract with exactly your dependencies, owned by you.

9
00:00:48.539 --> 00:00:54.991
Server schema sku_sales_input, physical type view: this is where your access views live.

10
00:00:55.041 --> 00:01:05.263
The server now points to sku_sales_input. The views do not exist yet: red.

11
00:01:05.313 --> 00:01:14.594
Create access views that expose exactly the contracted fields.

12
00:01:14.643 --> 00:01:19.595
Everything else in orders_v2 stays hidden from your data product.

13
00:01:19.645 --> 00:01:25.071
Apply the views.

14
00:01:25.121 --> 00:01:35.450
Test the consumer contract again: green.

15
00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:41.614
Change the owner: the purchasing analytics team owns this contract.

16
00:01:41.664 --> 00:01:46.579
The server points to sku_sales_input, where your access views live.

17
00:01:46.629 --> 00:01:54.665
With the views in place, the tests pass in the editor, too.

18
00:01:54.715 --> 00:02:03.411
Rebase your data product: read from sku_sales_input instead of orders_v2.

19
00:02:03.461 --> 00:02:08.982
Recreate the view.

20
00:02:09.032 --> 00:02:18.661
Your own consumers are unaffected: the SKU Sales tests stay green.

21
00:02:18.712 --> 00:02:23.662
The orders team can run your contract in their pipeline. That is the next exercise.
